  "id": "hemianesthesia",
  "term": "hemianesthesia",
  "definition": "Hemianesthesia is loss of feeling on one side of the body, usually up to the body's midline, and it may involve the skin, mucous membranes, muscles, and even deeper parts. In the historical account here, it is described especially in hysteria, where sensation may be reduced for pain or touch and may stay on one side or shift to the other.",
